CI vs CD – Most Engineers Get This Wrong

Many people say:
👉 “We have CI/CD”

But when you ask questions, the confusion starts.

Let’s simplify it 👇

🔹 Continuous Integration (CI)
Developers frequently merge code to a  shared repo
Automated build & test runs on every commit
 Goal: catch bugs early

🔹 Continuous Delivery (CD)
Code is always in a deployable state
 Deployment needs manual approval
 Used when control & compliance are important

🔹 Continuous Deployment (CD)
 Every successful change goes to  production automatically
 No manual intervention
 Used by mature DevOps teams

💡 CI is mandatory. CD depends on business, risk, and maturity.

In interviews, they don’t test definition
they test when and why you choose CI/CD.
